{% comment %}
  Identifies the delivery / room-of-choice / installation option group.

  That group gets special treatment on the PDP: it is pinned to the last position,
  numbered separately from the other groups, and forced to render as an accordion
  of swatches even when its option is configured as a Select. Three snippets
  depend on this test (product-options, cart-item-product-options and
  product-option-accordion), so the list of recognised titles lives here to keep
  them in agreement.

  Matching is exact against an allowlist rather than a substring like
  "room of choice", because a looser test also catches the FF-AGSL flooring
  group ("Delivery / Room of Choice / Flooring Installation Options"), which
  today renders as a plain dropdown in its natural position. Pulling that group
  into the pinned/accordion treatment is a deliberate change to those product
  pages, not a side effect of this test - add its title below when that change is
  actually wanted.

  Parameters:
    - category_title: the option group title (any case)

  Outputs 'true' when the group is the delivery group, otherwise nothing. Convert to
  a real boolean before use - an empty string is truthy in Liquid, so testing the
  captured value directly would match every group:
    {%- capture delivery_group_flag -%}
      {%- render 'is-delivery-option-group', category_title: category.title -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign delivery_group_flag = delivery_group_flag | strip -%}
    {%- assign is_delivery_group = false -%}
    {%- if delivery_group_flag == 'true' -%}
      {%- assign is_delivery_group = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign known_titles = 'assembly & room of choice installation needed?,delivery / room of choice / installation options' | split: ','
  assign candidate = category_title | downcase | strip
  for known_title in known_titles
    if candidate == known_title
      echo 'true'
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
